    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Unknown_Regions\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions\">Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions</a></i> </p><p>A prolific group of smugglers during the time of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/The_Old_Republic_Era\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"The Old Republic Era\">The Old Republic Era</a>, The Wavelength Gale often worked the edges of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/The_Outer_Rim\" title=\"The Outer Rim\">The Outer Rim</a>, and had a number of different havens and outposts scattered throughout <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/The_Unknown_Regions\" title=\"The Unknown Regions\">The Unknown Regions</a>, such as <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Volik\" title=\"Volik\">Volik</a>. </p><p>The Wavelength Gale installed a small landing beacon at the top of Mount Vorena, the tallest peak on the world. It is here that supposedly rests <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mask_of_Darth_Nihilus_(Sith_Artifact)\" title=\"The Mask of Darth Nihilus (Sith Artifact)\">The Mask of Darth Nihilus</a>, one of the most infamous Sith Artifacts in existence. </p>",
